clearcote r13 (Chromium 151): two fixes found by running the live audit against the r1 build.

1. element.idl no longer publishes fakeShadowRoot on Element.prototype. The name was the
   cheapest possible tell -- one in-operator check identified the build, with no reference
   data and nothing to compare against. Element::FakeShadowRoot() is kept in element.cc/h
   (it has no other caller) so the capability can be re-exposed behind a gated binding.

2. The persona claimed Chrome 150 on a 151 engine. Six sites across three files: the persona
   default major, the weighted version pool, its mirror in fingerprint_data.h, the default
   full version and the Edge UA version. Real 151 stable builds only.

Tail patch: every file here is already touched by 002/050/071/142/170, so the hunks are
expressed against the fully-applied stack.

--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/dom/element.idl
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/dom/element.idl
@@ -81,7 +81,11 @@
 
     [RaisesException, MeasureAs=ElementAttachShadow] ShadowRoot attachShadow(ShadowRootInit shadowRootInitDict);
     [PerWorldBindings, ImplementedAs=OpenShadowRoot] readonly attribute ShadowRoot? shadowRoot;
-    [PerWorldBindings, ImplementedAs=FakeShadowRoot] readonly attribute ShadowRoot? fakeShadowRoot;
+    // clearcote: fakeShadowRoot was a readonly attribute here. It is the cheapest possible
+    // tell -- `'fakeShadowRoot' in Element.prototype` identifies the build on any page, with
+    // nothing to compare against, and no shipping browser defines the name. Element::
+    // FakeShadowRoot() is kept in element.cc/h so the capability can be re-exposed behind a
+    // command-line-gated binding, but NO name is published on Element.prototype.
 
     [RaisesException] Element? closest(DOMString selectors);
     [RaisesException] boolean matches(DOMString selectors);
--- a/components/ungoogled/persona_profile.h
+++ b/components/ungoogled/persona_profile.h
@@ -63,8 +63,8 @@
   uint64_t persona_seed = 0;
 
   // ---- Identity ----
-  unsigned chrome_major_version = 150;
-  std::string chrome_full_version;  // e.g. "150.0.7871.114"
+  unsigned chrome_major_version = 151;
+  std::string chrome_full_version;  // e.g. "151.0.7922.108"
 
   // ---- Hardware (one tier: cores <-> RAM correlated) ----
   unsigned hardware_concurrency = 8;  // logical cores (navigator.hardwareConcurrency)
